<div style="background-color: #fef2f2; border: 1px solid #fecaca; border-left: 4px solid #dc2626; padding: 12px 15px; border-radius: 4px; margin-bottom: 25px;">
<p style="font-size: 9pt; font-weight: bold; color: #991b1b; text-transform: uppercase; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">⚠️ IMPORTANT NOTICE &amp; ENTRY ADVISORY</p>
<p style="font-size: 9pt; color: #7f1d1d; line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">This guide provides general operational guidelines. Final admission to Mexico is strictly decided by the Mexican National Migration Institute (INM) officer at the point of entry. Immigration requirements must be reassessed and verified for every single crew change before flight arrangements are finalized.</p>
</div>
<table style="margin-bottom: 25px;" border="0" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="border-bottom: 2px solid #2563eb; padding-bottom: 9px; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold; color: #1e293b; text-transform: uppercase;">📋 1. VISA ASSESSMENT &amp; QUALIFYING ALTERNATIVES</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="padding-top: 15px;">
<p style="font-size: 9pt; color: #334155; line-height: 1.6; text-align: justify; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">Visa requirements depend on the crew member's nationality and held travel documents. Official INM lists must be verified prior to booking flights.</p>
<div style="background-color: #f0fdf4; border: 1px solid #bbf7d0; border-left: 4px solid #16a34a; padding: 12px 15px; border-radius: 4px; margin-bottom: 15px;">
<p style="font-size: 9pt; font-weight: bold; color: #15803d; text-transform: uppercase; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">1.1 Nationals Exempt from Mexican Visa</p>
<ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 18px; font-size: 9pt; color: #166534; line-height: 1.5;">
<li>May enter Mexico as visitors without permission to engage in remunerated activities, subject to immigration review.</li>
<li>Must hold a valid original passport (minimum 6 months validity recommended).</li>
<li>Must demonstrate travel purpose (joining/leaving a vessel) with confirmed onward flight itinerary.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div style="background-color: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-left: 4px solid #0284c7; padding: 12px 15px; border-radius: 4px; margin-bottom: 15px;">
<p style="font-size: 9pt; font-weight: bold; color: #0369a1; text-transform: uppercase; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">1.2 Qualifying Alternatives to a Mexican Visa</p>
<p style="font-size: 8pt; color: #334155; line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">Nationals of visa-required countries may travel to Mexico without a Mexican visa if they hold any of the following valid documents:</p>
<ul style="margin: 0 0 10px 0; padding-left: 18px; font-size: 9pt; color: #334155; line-height: 1.5;">
<li><strong>Permanent Residence:</strong> Canada, United States, Japan, United Kingdom, Schengen Area countries, Chile, Colombia, or Peru.</li>
<li><strong>Valid / Unexpired Visa:</strong> Issued by Canada, Japan, United Kingdom, Schengen Area, or the <strong>United States of America</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>APEC Business Travel Card (ABTC):</strong> Approved by Mexico, when applicable.</li>
</ul>
<div style="background-color: #f0f9ff; border: 1px solid #bae6fd; border-radius: 4px; padding: 10px 12px; margin-top: 8px;">
<p style="font-size: 9pt; font-weight: bold; color: #0284c7; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">🇺🇸 Special Focus: U.S. C1/D1 Transit &amp; Crewmember Visas</p>
<p style="font-size: 9pt; color: #0f172a; line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">&bull; <strong>Acceptance as Visa Alternative:</strong> Under Mexican immigration rules, a valid U.S. Visa (including B1/B2, C1, D, or combined <strong>C1/D1 Crewmember Transit Visas</strong>) qualifies as an eligible alternative to enter Mexico as a visitor/seafarer without needing a separate Mexican visa.<br>&bull; <strong>U.S. Flight Connections:</strong> If the seafarer's flight itinerary includes domestic or transit connections through any U.S. airport, holding a valid <strong>C1/D1 or C1 visa</strong> is mandatory for U.S. TSA / CBP transit clearance before reaching Mexico.<br>&bull; <strong>Verification Requirement:</strong> The U.S. C1/D1 visa must be valid, unexpired, and stamped in a valid passport at the time of entry into Mexico.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div style="background-color: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; padding: 12px 15px; border-radius: 4px;">
<p style="font-size: 9pt; font-weight: bold; color: #1e293b; text-transform: uppercase; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">1.3 Mandatory Documents for Seafarers Arriving by Air</p>
