<div style="background-color: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; border-left: 4px solid #0284c7; padding: 12px 15px; border-radius: 4px;">
<p style="font-size: 9pt; font-weight: bold; color: #0369a1; text-transform: uppercase; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">Customs vs. Immigration Requirements:</p>
<p style="font-size: 9pt; color: #334155; line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">Immigration and Customs requirements are completely separate. Crew members should travel strictly with personal luggage. The following items MUST be disclosed to ISS Mexico in advance:</p>
<ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 18px; font-size: 9pt; color: #334155; line-height: 1.5;">
<li>Ship spares, tools, equipment, medicines, or vessel stores.</li>
<li>Large cash amounts or negotiable financial instruments.</li>
<li>Alcohol, tobacco products, or restricted goods.</li>
<li>Any item intended for delivery to or removal from the vessel.</li>
</ul>
<p style="font-size: 9pt; color: #64748b; font-style: italic; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;">*Note: Do not quote fixed fines or guarantee customs admission. Customs treatment depends on item type, quantity, docs, and authority evaluation.</p>
</div>
